# User Rules (snapshot)

These were cloud User Rules active in Cursor Customize at export time. Edit as needed for this project.

## Committing changes with git

Only create commits when requested by the user. If unclear, ask first. When creating a new git commit:

- NEVER update the git config
- NEVER run destructive/irreversible git commands unless explicitly requested
- NEVER skip hooks unless explicitly requested
- NEVER force push to main/master without warning
- Avoid `git commit --amend` except under the documented safe conditions
- NEVER commit unless explicitly asked
- Pass commit messages via HEREDOC
- Do not push unless explicitly asked

## Creating pull requests

Use `gh` for GitHub tasks. Parallel status/diff/log checks before creating PR. Push with `-u` if needed. Create PR with HEREDOC body (Summary + Test plan). Return the PR URL.

## Frontend design

Follow the project's frontend design hard rules (composition, brand-first, typography, hero budget, cards policy, avoid AI-default palettes). Preserve existing design systems when working in one.

## Final response communication

Communicate directly and concisely. Prefer pointed responses. Bold sparingly. Keep concise unless thorough detail is requested.
